# Git branching workflow

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `main` | Stable / production only. **Do not merge here unless the user explicitly says to.** |
| `develop` | Integration branch. All finished feature work lands here. |
| `feature/*` | One change set per branch (e.g. `feature/hero-motion`). |

## Every change

1. Start from latest `develop` (not `main`).
2. Create / switch to a **feature branch** for the work.
3. Commit on that feature branch as you go.
4. When the feature is done, **merge it into `develop`** (fast-forward or merge commit).
5. Do **not** merge into `main` until the user asks.

## Agent must

- Never commit directly on `main` or `develop` for feature work — use a feature branch first.
- After finishing a feature branch, merge it into `develop` automatically.
- Leave `main` unchanged unless the user explicitly requests a release/merge to `main`.
- Follow the user rules for commit message style and safety (no force-push to main, no `--no-verify`, etc.).

## Naming

- Features: `feature/<short-kebab-description>`
- Fixes: `fix/<short-kebab-description>`

